<title>USA: Ohio EPA gives nod to BP Toledo refinery upgrades.</title>
<headline>Ohio EPA gives nod to BP Toledo refinery upgrades.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ohio Environmental Protection Agency issued a final air permit Monday for British Petroleum to modify its Toledo refinery to process heavy sour crudes.</p>
<p>The permit will allow BP to add two new sulphur recovery units, a new coker furnace and a new coker, and modify its hydrogen furnace and coke handling equipment.</p>
<p>The modifications will allow BP to process crude oil from Canada that has a higher sulphur content, helping raise profitability at the 148,000 barrel per day refinery.</p>
<p>-- Matt Daily +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
